            "role": "heading",
            "order": 0,
            "content": "SST in miniature"
          },
          {
            "@type": "SstAtom",
            "hash": "b52c1ccfa6d6d1f7daad3a9535b7ff255d078b84fb1c0b668af7cc307acff97b",
            "role": "subtitle",
            "order": 1,
            "content": "The same content, two faces, one identity"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "@type": "SstBlock",
        "hash": "ed74b0559afa27aee630d29e21bdf1ade0872bb6d743544a5d87247dee68448b",
        "page": "paper",
        "section": "abstract",
        "name": "body",
        "order": 2,
        "block_type": "paragraph",
        "atoms": [
          {
            "@type": "SstAtom",
            "hash": "a7d1e27b19a7d3815fa810206dc2684ed734021b890b5af6fd8b637272e7b593",
            "role": "body",
            "order": 0,
            "content": "Every piece of content on this page is an atom: a sentence-level unit whose identity is the SHA-256 hash of its normalized text."
          },
          {
            "@type": "SstAtom",
            "hash": "ab001c7421818cc1145721f09da425f50ad4b57ec975d0087c852e0be9a87fac",
            "role": "body",
            "order": 1,
            "content": "Atoms compose into blocks, blocks into pages, and each level's identity is a Merkle root over its children — change one character anywhere and every fingerprint above it changes."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "@type": "SstBlock",
        "hash": "5d36dd081432942407dff69b4d35a63713f2e826039aebfb3918880a5d10e15e",
        "name": "body",
        "block_type": "paragraph",
        "atoms": [
          {
            "@type": "SstAtom",
            "hash": "24ba05aafcb93017f113408b406040d8321b9e1d6df2e418127f6d325e590fc0",
            "role": "body",
            "order": 0,
            "content": "The page you are reading is Dual-Native: the human face is this rendered HTML; the machine face is a JSON-LD manifest in the head carrying the same atoms with their hashes."
          },
          {
            "@type": "SstAtom",
            "hash": "ffcc6da6beff701d844539048330448d6280df6a769b735982bc1938c8b29617",
            "role": "body",
            "order": 1,
            "content": "The manifest is derived from the rendered page, never maintained by hand — the two faces cannot drift, because one is computed from the other at build time."
          },
          {
            "@type": "SstAtom",
            "hash": "888a9cc024f3b2c5a493e03a16a9ee6f0820e9cf5448c15904b794042b8cf459",
            "role": "body",
            "order": 2,
            "content": "Anyone can verify this page without trusting its publisher: re-hash the visible text, recompute the Merkle roots, and compare against the manifest. The artefact carries its own proof."
          },
          {
            "@type": "SstAtom",
            "hash": "32dc5c895df741fbb58296dccb7420967926e611af0d069e9d7ef6b79ae206b0",
            "role": "body",
            "order": 3,
            "content": "A charter in the head declares the operator's terms: who may read, quote, ingest, or train on this content. Sovereignty is data, not a request."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "@type": "SstBlock",
        "hash": "29dbaa9fb189721f41cf2a35b49d488d534de74e4b7b6c6bef4d1afd6bc616bb",
        "page": "paper",
        "section": "method",
        "name": "body",
        "order": 4,
        "block_type": "paragraph",
        "atoms": [
          {
            "@type": "SstAtom",
            "hash": "b698b818022a138bd9649937afce35c173eed2a09a557eed8dc152e92567fe93",
            "role": "body",
            "order": 0,
            "content": "Run the verifier against this very file to watch all six gates pass; flip a single character and watch them fail."
          },
          {
            "@type": "SstAtom",
            "hash": "b917c532d7264e33d4cabbf8b0ee81ae6ac5951b06ac9bdc5cee78ccbb2e0fc3",
            "role": "body",
            "order": 1,
            "content": "This entire implementation is one dependency-free script — the point of SST is not machinery, it is that identity, composition, and verification are simple enough to fit in it."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "@type": "SstBlock",
        "hash": "8fed109f02c4333ba7a77208ca2087e3ad703ff9d73df31a49ea7d46167be517",
        "page": "paper",
        "section": "geometry",
        "name": "body",
        "order": 5,
        "block_type": "paragraph",
        "atoms": [
          {
            "@type": "SstAtom",
            "hash": "f832fb1c9b42fc5c68c3e7f1fe09292275976461142ccc5419632e023de70fb4",
            "role": "body",
            "order": 0,
            "content": "Beyond the content lies the geometry: a second Merkle root over every declared site — present or vacant — so the shape of what is missing is provable, not merely asserted."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "@type": "SstBlock",
        "hash": "2ec0cb788cd320b69bde7d36d5f64c7727fe38bc3851c4f6389ef041ef033f66",
        "page": "paper",
        "name": "note",
        "block_type": "paragraph",
        "atoms": [
          {
            "@type": "SstAtom",
            "hash": "f1e13c0c4bb2f8899ef884137689300f66e1bbb4e0829042b64eae6b1b94c9ae",
            "role": "body",
            "order": 0,
            "content": "This paragraph is one identity at two coordinates, printed twice on this page and listed once in the manifest: a bill of what the page carries, never a transcript of where."
          }
        ]
      }
